  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 60af0432a3c869e48a591344a8dafd71, type: 3}
  m_Name: PreCare 1
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  question: "You and other caregivers have shared how treatment-related nerve pain
    can make it hard for patients to do daily tasks\u2014sometimes long after treatment
    ends. A research team designing a preclinical study decides to track nerve-related
    side effects when testing new drug compounds.\n\n<b>Caregiver input can help
    researchers improve how they design preclinical studies.</b>\n\nIs this <b>true</b>
    or <b>false</b>?"
  explanation: "When caregivers share how treatments affect everyday life\u2014like
    nerve pain that makes walking or using hands difficult\u2014researchers can use
    that insight to plan better preclinical studies. By tracking these side effects
    early on, research teams can focus on treatments that not only fight cancer but
    also reduce long-term impacts on daily living for patients and families."
  correctAnswer: True
  incorrectAnswer1: False
  incorrectAnswer2: 
  incorrectAnswer3: 
  questionRole: Caregiver
  questionType: TrueFalse
  questionStage: PreClinical
